From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lethalbas <lethalbas@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:45:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rt(engine,tse): make ray tracing runtime-optional in the TSE
 engine

Replays e62b6fcc onto SamTSE: delay-loaded RayTracedGL1.dll with the
RTGL1Loader probe, non-fatal RT adapter enumeration (Adapter.cpp applies
cleanly despite the 10-line TFE/TSE difference), and the Release|x64
Engine.vcxproj additions (RT sources, RTGL1 include/lib, delayimp,
RG_USE_SURFACE_WIN32). The vcxproj hunks were re-applied by hand because
TSE's PreprocessorDefinitions lack FIRST_ENCOUNTER, so the TFE context
did not match.

Ported code: Serious-Engine-RT (https://github.com/sultim-t/Serious-Engine-RT,
GPL-2.0-only) by Sultim Tsyrendashiev; original copyright notices kept.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
